# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .codx generated data plane — NEVER tracked.
#
# .codx holds two different things: shared artifacts a human edits and the team
# shares through git (profiles, tasks, boards, views, teams, workspaces) and the
# state the platform generates while it runs (chat turns, browser sessions, the
# harness audit journal, orchestration/board state, rebuildable indexes).
#
# The generated half is unbounded, model-influenced and untrusted: one tool
# output that prints a token would otherwise enter git history forever. It is
# runtime state, it is not source code, and it is not committed.
#
# Keep in sync with codx/junior/runtime.py: DATA_PLANE_ENTRIES —
# api/tests/security/ciso_repo_check.py fails when the two lists diverge.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.codx/chat_turns/
.codx/browser_sessions/
.codx/browser_downloads/
.codx/computer_downloads/
.codx/computer_library/
.codx/harness/
.codx/orchestration/
.codx/board_manager/
.codx/autonomy/
.codx/atlas/
.codx/db/
.codx/logs/
.codx/tmp/
.codx/cache/
.codx/dependency_graph.json
.codx/domain_map.json
.codx/project_summary.md
.codx/wiki_settings.json
**/.codx/wiki_settings.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scratch space and generated wiki state — never tracked.
#
# ``tmp/`` is where ad-hoc scripts and commit-message drafts are written while
# working; keeping them in git published host paths and half-finished probes.
# ``wiki/update_status.json`` is rewritten by the wiki builder on every file
# change and only holds absolute paths, so it is machine state, not content.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/tmp/
wiki/update_status.json
